[s1] NXP Semiconductors Reports Third Quarter 2026 Results
[s2] Announces $5 Billion Increase in Share Repurchase Authorization
[s3] EINDHOVEN, The Netherlands, October 27, 2026 – NXP Semiconductors N.V. (NASDAQ: NXPI) today reported financial results for the third quarter, which ended September 27, 2026.
[s4] “NXP delivered third-quarter revenue of $3.8 billion, up 19 percent year-on-year and 8 percent sequentially.
[s5] Strong profitability leading to free cash flow generation enables NXP to invest in innovative solutions and expand manufacturing capabilities that support our long-term growth objectives, while continuing to return capital to shareholders through our newly announced $5 billion share repurchase authorization.
[s6] Key Highlights for the Third Quarter 2026:
[s7] Revenue was $3.79 billion, up 19 percent year-on-year;
[s8] GAAP gross margin was 57.8 percent, GAAP operating margin was 32.4 percent and GAAP diluted Net Income per Share was $3.48;
[s9] Non-GAAP gross margin was 58.6 percent, non-GAAP operating margin was 37.1 percent, and non-GAAP diluted Net Income per Share was $4.20;
[s10] Cash flow from operations was $1.26 billion, with net capex investments of $50 million, resulting in non-GAAP free cash flow of $1.21 billion or 31.9 percent of revenue;
[s11] Capital return during the quarter was $359 million, representing 29.8 percent of third quarter non-GAAP free cash flow. Dividends paid during the quarter were $256 million, and share buybacks were $103 million;
[s12] On August 4, 2026, NXP announced that its Trimension™ Ultra-Wideband (UWB) ranging and radar solutions will be deployed by the BMW Group across its fleet, starting with selected 2026 vehicle programs;
[s13] On August 12, 2026, NXP broke ground on its assembly and test site expansion in Malaysia;
[s14] On September 28, 2026, VSMC, the joint venture between Vanguard International Semiconductor Corporation (VIS) and NXP Semiconductors N.V., marked the grand opening of its first 300mm fab in Singapore; and
[s15] The NXP Board of Directors, in October after quarter end, authorized a $5 billion share repurchase program in addition to the $1.3 billion remaining under the prior authorization.
